Batch.Works, a London-based company specialising in Circular Manufacturing, demonstrates innovative circular practises through the utilisation of 3D printing technology. The organisation aims to revolutionise conventional manufacturing by repurposing disposable plastic waste into marketable products for international brands and designers. The case study highlights the efforts of a UK retailer in tackling plastic waste issues. They were awarded a £15,000 grant to create and test a service that transforms plastic waste into marketable products. This initiative involved addressing challenges such as sourcing materials, refining processes, and implementing cultural changes within the retailer's operations. Batch.Works demonstrates a strong dedication to sustainability and innovation by spearheading efforts to redefine manufacturing processes, effectively combining environmental responsibility with advanced techniques.